<%#
  A single terminal command. It used to render as two adjacent pills — a `$`
  chip beside a `<code>` chip — which read as boxes inside a box once code
  blocks became a mauve field of their own.

  It is a real `<pre><code>` now, so it takes the same field, radius, scrollbar
  and Copy button as every other code block on the site, and the prompt is
  muted and unselectable exactly as Rouge's own `.gp` token is. One code
  language, however the block got here.
%>

<div class="not-prose">
  <pre><code><span class="select-none text-mauve-11">$ </span><%= content.to_s.strip %></code></pre>
</div>
